UTDeck (stage 5.1): a phone's battery.

MangoHud took only power supplies with "BAT" in their name (laptops' BAT0); a phone's is called
"battery", so the overlay found none. A supply the kernel marks as type "Battery" is taken too,
except a device's own (a controller's battery has scope "Device"). MangoHud keeps two batteries and
did not check that limit; it does now. Its power figure preferred power_now, which on the Nothing
Phone (1) is in another unit (67.5 W while charging at 0.35 A and 4.28 V, which is 1.5 W): current
times voltage comes first now, power_now only without them.

